.TH CPU-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-20" "cpu-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpu-revamped \- load, temperature and clock in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpu-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cpu-revamped
shows how busy the CPU is in the tmux status line, with its temperature, its
clock, the three load averages, the core count, a graph of the recent
samples, the busiest process and the governor. macOS is read from iostat,
top, sysctl and, for the temperature, macmon, osx-cpu-temp or istats. Linux
is read from /proc and sysfs, with sensors as the last resort for the
temperature.
.PP
The entry point
.B cpu-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup key in one tmux call
and replaces the placeholders #{cpu_percentage}, #{cpu_icon},
#{cpu_fg_color}, #{cpu_bg_color}, #{cpu_temp}, #{cpu_temp_icon},
#{cpu_temp_fg_color}, #{cpu_temp_bg_color}, #{cpu_freq}, #{cpu_load},
#{cpu_load5}, #{cpu_load15}, #{cpu_count}, #{cpu_graph}, #{cpu_top_process},
#{cpu_governor}, #{cpu_load_color}, #{cpu_alert}, #{cpu_cores}, #{cpu_sep_left},
#{cpu_sep_right} and #{cpu_throttle} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored sample at once. When the sample is older
than the interval it starts one in the background, so the status line never
waits. The temperature, the clock, the load averages, the busiest process,
the governor and the throttling flag are read only for a placeholder the
status line uses, at the detail interval, and the per-core load at every
sample. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a
menu.
.PP
On Linux the load is the busy share of two reads of /proc/stat taken 0.3
seconds apart, with iowait counted as idle. On macOS it is a hundred less
the idle share of iostat, or of top when iostat is missing. The clock on
Apple Silicon is looked up from the chip generation. #{cpu_governor} is
empty on macOS, which has none.
.PP
#{cpu_cores} prints one bar per core, from the same eight bars as
#{cpu_graph}, each the busy share of that core since the previous sample.
Linux reads the cpuN lines of /proc/stat and keeps the counters in an option.
macOS reads host_processor_info through JXA, run by osascript, and falls back
to macmon. The first sample has no previous counters and prints nothing, and
two samples in the same second keep the previous bars.
.PP
#{cpu_throttle} prints @cpu_revamped_throttle_icon while the CPU is held back.
Linux counts it from a rise of any thermal_throttle count in sysfs since the
previous sample. macOS counts it from pmset reporting a CPU speed limit under
100 or a thermal warning level above nominal.
.PP
#{cpu_sep_left} and #{cpu_sep_right} print powerline arrows styled with the
background of the load tier as their foreground, over
@cpu_revamped_sep_bg.
.PP
An icon, a label or a text set to off prints nothing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the popup key and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored sample: percentage, icon, fg_color, bg_color, temp, temp_icon, temp_fg_color, temp_bg_color, freq, load, load5, load15, count, graph, top_process, governor, load_color, alert, cores, sep_left, sep_right or throttle. The status line runs it, and it starts a sample in the background when the stored one is older than the interval.
.TP
.B refresh
Sample the CPU now, read the details the status line uses, store the sample and say how much of the CPU is busy.
.TP
.B card
Read everything now and print one row per figure: the load, the temperature, the clock, the load averages, the cores, the governor, the busiest process and the history.
.TP
.B popup
Open a CPU monitor in a tmux popup: the popup command, else btop, else htop, else top. The popup key runs it. A command that is not installed is named in a message, and a tmux older than 3.2 says so.
.TP
.B daemon
Sample the CPU and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per interval, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the popup, each tool or file a figure comes from, the monitor the popup opens, the key it found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-top\-process\-label .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the popup key and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI CPU_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR CPU_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B CPU_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B CPU_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B CPU_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B CPU_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the monitor popup. off binds nothing. The default is M\-c, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_popup_width
The width of the popup, as tmux reads it. The default is 80%.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_popup_height
The height of the popup. The default is 80%.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_popup_command
The command the popup runs, with its arguments. The default is btop, else htop, else top.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_interval
Seconds a sample stays fresh before the CPU is read again. The default is 5.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_detail_interval
Seconds the temperature, the clock, the load averages, the busiest process, the governor and the throttling flag stay fresh. The default is 60.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_throttle_when_detached
1 stops sampling while no client is attached; the status line keeps the last sample. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_render
jobs turns each placeholder into a call the status line runs. options turns it into a read of a tmux option that the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. Any other value means jobs. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_medium_thresh
Load percent at which the tier becomes medium. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_high_thresh
Load percent at which the tier becomes high, and at which #{cpu_alert} prints. The default is 80.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_medium_thresh
Degrees Celsius at which the temperature tier becomes medium. The default is 65.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_high_thresh
Degrees Celsius at which the temperature tier becomes high, and at which #{cpu_alert} prints. The default is 80.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load_medium_ratio
Load average per core at which #{cpu_load_color} becomes medium. The default is 0.7.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load_high_ratio
Load average per core at which #{cpu_load_color} becomes high. The default is 1.0.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_low_icon
What #{cpu_icon} prints in the low tier. off prints nothing. The default is one bar of three.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_medium_icon
What #{cpu_icon} prints in the medium tier. The default is two bars of three.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_high_icon
What #{cpu_icon} prints in the high tier. The default is three bars.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_low_fg_color
The style #{cpu_fg_color} and #{cpu_load_color} print in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_medium_fg_color
The style they print in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_high_fg_color
The style they print in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_low_bg_color
The style #{cpu_bg_color} prints in the low tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_medium_bg_color
The style #{cpu_bg_color} prints in the medium tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_high_bg_color
The style #{cpu_bg_color} prints in the high tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_low_icon
What #{cpu_temp_icon} prints in the low temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_medium_icon
What #{cpu_temp_icon} prints in the medium temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_high_icon
What #{cpu_temp_icon} prints in the high temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_low_fg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_fg_color} prints in the low temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_medium_fg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_fg_color} prints in the medium temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_high_fg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_fg_color} prints in the high temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_low_bg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_bg_color} prints in the low temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_medium_bg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_bg_color} prints in the medium temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_high_bg_color
The style #{cpu_temp_bg_color} prints in the high temperature tier. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_alert_icon
What #{cpu_alert} prints while the load or the temperature is at its high threshold. off prints nothing. The default is !.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_throttle_icon
What #{cpu_throttle} prints while the CPU is held back. off prints nothing. The default is throttled.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_notify
1 sends a desktop notification when throttling starts, once per episode and again only after it ended. It needs #{cpu_throttle} in the status line. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_sep_left
What #{cpu_sep_left} prints. off prints nothing. The default is the left powerline arrow.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_sep_right
What #{cpu_sep_right} prints. off prints nothing. The default is the right powerline arrow.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_sep_bg
The background colour behind both arrows. The default is default.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_unit
C prints the temperature in Celsius, F in Fahrenheit. The default is C.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_percentage_format
printf format of #{cpu_percentage}. The default is %s%%.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_format
printf format of #{cpu_temp}. The default is %s, the degree sign and the unit.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_freq_format
printf format of #{cpu_freq}, in megahertz. The default is %sMHz.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load_format
printf format of #{cpu_load}, #{cpu_load5} and #{cpu_load15}. The default is %s.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_icons
ascii labels nothing. nerd puts a Nerd Font glyph before every metric that takes a label. The default is ascii.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_fixed_width
on pads each figure on the left to its natural width, so a change from 9% to 42% does not shift the status line. The default is off.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_percentage_label
Text printed before the load percent, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_label
Text printed before the temperature, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_freq_label
Text printed before the clock, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load_label
Text printed before the one minute load average, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load5_label
Text printed before the five minute load average, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load15_label
Text printed before the fifteen minute load average, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_count_label
Text printed before the core count, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_graph_label
Text printed before the graph, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_top_process_label
Text printed before the busiest process, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_governor_label
Text printed before the governor, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_cores_label
Text printed before the per-core bars, only when the value is not empty. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_percentage_width
Characters the load percent is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_temp_width
Characters the temperature is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_freq_width
Characters the clock is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load_width
Characters the one minute load average is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load5_width
Characters the five minute load average is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_load15_width
Characters the fifteen minute load average is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_count_width
Characters the core count is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_graph_width
Characters the graph is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_top_process_width
Characters the busiest process is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_governor_width
Characters the governor is padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @cpu_revamped_cores_width
Characters the per-core bars are padded to on the left. A longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored sample lives in
.BR @cpu_revamped_percent ,
.BR _temp ,
.BR _freq ,
.BR _load ,
.BR _load5 ,
.BR _load15 ,
.BR _count ,
.BR _governor ,
.BR _top_process ,
.BR _cores ,
.BR _cores_stat ,
.BR _throttle ,
.BR _throttle_count ,
.BR _notified
and
.BR _history ,
with the time of each reading in options that end in _ts. apply records the
placeholders the status line uses in
.BR @cpu_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @cpu_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @cpu_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR iostat (8),
.BR sysctl (8),
.BR proc (5),
.BR gum (1)
